			"SHA": "fa903600e15697c37927ddae2bfa35a3cbd7ab31"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T22:42:22Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				4
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Rename user-data directory root from .land to .fiddee\n\nAfter the product rebranding to FIDDEE, the hardcoded `$HOME/.land/...` path literals scattered across Cocoon, Output, and Wind were inconsistent with the new product identity. Normalise all references to `$HOME/.fiddee/...` so the user-data directory mirrors the product name.\n\nCocoon (+1 commit): Extract the FIDDEE user-data path into a shared `FiddeeRoot()` atom at Source/Platform/FiddeeRoot.ts, mirroring the Rust atom in Mountain. Replace hardcoded `$HOME/.land` prefixes in Extension Context.ts, Host Handler.ts (extensionStorage, globalStorage, logs), and add `/.fiddee/extensions/` to the extension-bug frame matcher in Notification Handler.ts. All ESBuild Target/ artifacts rebuilt.\n\nOutput (+1 commit): Update all documentation comments and inline `Why` strings in Pipeline.ts, Plugin Index.ts, Extension Gallery Service.ts, and Icon Stylesheet URL rewriter.ts to reference `~/.fiddee/extensions/` instead of `~/.land/extensions/`. Compiled bundles and source maps regenerated.\n\nWind (+1 commit): Update the inline comment in ResolveConfiguration referencing `~/.land/workspaces/RecentlyOpened.json` to `~/.fiddee/workspaces/RecentlyOpened.json`.\n\nMountain (+1 commit): Synchronised to matching HEAD — no functional delta for this change.\n\nTogether these changes ensure a single source of truth for the product data directory path across the TypeScript layers, with new code reading from `FiddeeRoot()` and all stale documentation strings corrected.",
			"SHA": "b953180e3e03fd1e284ed751416d908d7c6b60a8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T22:23:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Wire workspace save methods and fix Tauri IPC fallback in Wind\n\nAdvance Cocoon, Mountain, and Wind submodules to collectively enable `vscode.workspace.save()` / `saveAll()` / `saveAs()` from extensions and fix two workbench boot crash categories in Wind.\n\n**Mountain (+1 commit, feat):** Add three new IPC handler arms to the Workspace dispatch table in `CreateEffectForRequest` — `Workspace.Save`, `Workspace.SaveAs`, and `Workspace.SaveAll` (including the legacy `saveAll` method name used by gRPC/Client.ts). All three degrade gracefully when Sky has no handler registered, logging a warning and returning the original URI (for Save/SaveAs) or null (for SaveAll) instead of crashing the extension host.\n\n**Cocoon (+1 commit, chore):** Rebuild all 39 `Target/` ESBuild bundles and regenerate the `RouteManifest` to track the four new Mountain RPC methods, raising `MountainMethods` count from 130 to 134 with a generation timestamp of `2026-05-19T22:15:03Z`.\n\n**Wind (+1 commit, fix):** Fix two boot-time crash sources in `ResolveConfiguration` — (1) add `(window as any).__TAURI_INTERNALS__?.invoke` to the fallback chain before the `__TAURI__` variants so the Tauri IPC bridge is found in Tauri v2 webview contexts; (2) replace all `|| undefined` path fallbacks (homeDir, tmpDir, userDataDir, logsPath) with concrete defaults like `/tmp/.fiddee` so `path.posix.join(undefined, 'User')` no longer throws \"The path argument must be of type string\" during workbench initialisation. Propagate the fallback to `extensionsPath` via `userDataDir` so extension scanning never receives undefined.\n\nTogether these changes complete the workspace document save IPC round-trip from Cocoon through Mountain to Sky, while hardening Wind against Tauri version mismatch and missing IPC responses at startup.",
			"SHA": "bbd041b6c55c90b3e0432757dbf463009fc6e181"
		}
	],
